# rm381, the dipping-cup boat (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm381
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_roald_toft
written_by codex
title the dipping-cup boat
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk whittles_small_hulls_to_try_in_a_dipping_cup
likes pickled_herring whittling festival_bells first_warm_day
dislikes salt_wind wet_floors
fears confusing_a_whisper_with_a_witness
hopes one_little_boat_that_sails_straight
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.5 gossip -0.5 weather +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=withheld refuse=frank tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hums a sea air to thumb-sized boats and keeps a dry, folded list beyond reach of the steam.

words
oath! = Scald my hull | Sink my shallow ladle
saying! = A dipping cup makes an honest sound | A secret floats best without a sail
bed = a berth on dry cloth | a good length of blanket
wind = salt on the breath | a biting sea breeze
work = a proper turn at it | the day's decent part
quiet = a hush after splashing | a still moment
tale = a sea air with words | a tune turned into a tale
hull = a hollowed chip | a smooth little hull
cup = a deep dipping cup | a little bath of tin
bottom = a flat bottom | a rounded keel
towel = a thick cloth | a fold of fresh linen
herring = a thin pickled strip | a curl of herring
chip = a pale shaving | a twist of wood
lip = a raised rim | a worn brim

any
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Clean water goes cloudy with surprisingly little stirred up from below. I reserve judgement about clean uniforms too.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : Fine doors can shut away more than steam. I like particulars before I speak.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Warmth and food both get into a wolf more easily through an open door.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A dry towel can be offered before learning somebody's whole history.
opinion @1 city for 1 : A city that makes room for washing and for dreaming is tolerably well arranged.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : Respectable work doesn't absolve a seller from giving the actual measure.

grown
line @1 greet : There's a dry corner by my humming. | Welcome in a lower voice.
line @1 greet.return : And a little warmth round your greeting.
line @1 again.open : Come round the cup again already.
line @1 farewell : A dry landing when your next journey ends. | Keep the wind off your wet sleeve.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll return your wish with the towel still warm.
line @1 react.news : Tell it in air clear of steam. | I'll let the tune fall quiet.
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't heard that beneath the tune.
line @1 react.news.known : I know the waterline on that account.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Something in that telling won't float straight.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'll keep the little boats still for news of a loss.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's a light piece of news to carry.
line @1 ask.how : Did the day leave a moment for your own thoughts?
line @1 answer.how : I'm afloat with a quiet bit of room.
line @1 sympathise : You can sit without having to whistle up a reason.
line @1 reassure : A small vessel can right itself once the water settles.
line @1 refuse : I've something in my keeping that needs attention first.
line @1 accept_decline : Quite understood. Your time hasn't been taken on hire.
line @1 preclose : I'd best attend to my bit of dry business.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while you can still walk at your own speed.
line @1 ack : Yes. Quite clear below the surface.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I watch for the steam to thin. | I leave the dry things within reach of the warm things.
b : To shut the door? | Won't they grow damp?
a : To judge whether to fetch a fresh towel. | A short reach. A very deliberate space between.

scene exchange2
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This hull fits a dipping cup. | I carve the inside first.
b : Does it float? | Isn't the outside easier?
a : It shows me where the next shaving should come off. | It's tempting to finish a beautiful boat with nowhere to sit.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A herring curled up in vinegar reminds me of a small harbour. | I like pickled fish after steam.
b : Which part is the harbour? | A sharper taste?
a : The curl. The vinegar sits inside it like water at a quay. | A very clear one. The tongue wakes first.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a festival bell behind my hum. | A bell outlasts its own sound.
b : How can you do that? | In the ear?
a : Hold its last note in mind and fit the tune beneath it. | In the way my paw goes on carving to that time.

scene exchange5
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Spring's first soft afternoon makes the bath steam almost invisible. | I take a little boat into the light when spring warms.
b : Too warm outside? | To sail it outdoors?
a : Just warm enough to make the water look wonderfully still. | To see which scratches winter concealed.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind puts a rough edge on the lip of a cup. | I let the tune have the sea and keep the wind away.
b : Can you taste it? | Wish it were still?
a : Even after wiping. I take the cup inside. | Still enough to see what the little hull does by itself.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet floor's a poor place to come dreaming ashore. | I dry a track just wider than my towel.
b : Have you slipped? | Why so narrow?
a : I learned the careful step the quick way. | Better one wholly dry path than a handsome damp room.

scene exchange8
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a private list of certain arrangements. | My plainest paper has the most careful fold.
b : What arrangements? | May I see it?
a : Things I think worth remembering until I know more. | Plainly speaking, no.

scene exchange9
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put my best little hull in #self.friend#'s keeping. | A friend needn't hear every note I'm humming.
b : Do you want it back? | Which ones stay quiet?
a : I'd rather see it tried on another stretch of water. | Usually the ones I haven't decided how to end.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A respectable post entails an extraordinary number of damp corners. | I'd rather make a dry place properly than name it grandly.
b : What makes it worth the trouble? | Do customers notice?
a : Fresh cloth going into cold paws. | Cold toes notice the difference straight away.

scene exchange11
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The report was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard it over the splashing. | A whisper lingers in steam longer than a song.
b : Can you certify the account? | Does it improve with age?
a : Only for the words reaching me. | It improves most by thinning to nothing.

scene exchange12
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Even warm water gets carefully measured in a lean week. | A lean purse still deserves proper leisure to wash.
b : Does comfort shrink with the bucket? | Would you hurry a visitor?
a : Not if one takes care with the cloth too. | I can spend the same courtesy on different purses.

scene exchange13
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my knife and my paper on different shelves. | My little fleet sleeps on folded linen.
b : Afraid of a slip? | Will it sail in dreams?
a : Afraid of oil spread over a perfectly legible note. | I own the dreams readily. The fleet remains discreet.

scene exchange14
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum the rowing part on uphill walks. | I like a town street with a distant water sound.
b : Does it pull you along? | Homesick for the Sound?
a : It settles my feet into a shared pace. | For its rhythm. Salt in my ears is quite another thing.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to launch one hull and watch it go straight. | I'd build a perfect toy ship from a plain stick.
b : No sails? | What makes it perfect?
a : Then the wood could claim all the credit. | A wake exactly the width it ought to leave.

scene exchange16
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ease my carving thumb in a cup of warm water. | A hum gets rough if I don't pause between verses.
b : Does the wood hurt? | Do you mind a pause?
a : I hold it harder than necessary when I start dreaming. | The sounds of the room return in that gap.

scene exchange17
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A quiet thanks after washing comes easily. | I can be grateful for a safe door without admiring everything behind it.
b : Grateful for the water? | A difficult distinction?
a : And for having somewhere to sit while I dry. | A necessary one in this city.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I flatten the towel before starting a tune. | I stop carving as soon as the light blurs the grain.
b : Why the order? | Afraid of your blade?
a : I lose the corners when my ears wander. | Fond of my thumb, which is much the same precaution.

story tale1 [topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling]
  : My first little hull rolled over as soon as it touched water. I took it out and gave the upturned base a long inspection.
  : It resembled a quite handsome seal, floating with its nose up.
  b : Did you cut a new keel?
  : I gave it eyes and carved a second boat. The seal's kept a remarkably steady course ever since.

story tale2 [topic=memories]
  : I folded a blank scrap round a particularly private page. Steam reached the outside and printed the inner ink faintly backwards.
  : I turned the damp leaves to the lamp. It looked like a list written for fish under a pond.
  b : Could a passer-by read it?
  : I couldn't, and I knew the order. I dried both leaves and improved my choice of shelf.

story tale3 [topic=food]
  : I ate pickled herring beside one of my little ships and learnt the danger of admiring two curved things at once.
  : My paw was carrying salt towards the ship when the grain caught my eye.
  b : Did you varnish the herring instead?
  : I ate it promptly and cleared a sensible distance between my workshop and my plate.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry cloth where the warm walk finishes. | Stow the spill bucket clear of the heel.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A low note before the water gets noisy. | The first cupful deserves a clean rim.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep a dry outer fold on that page. | Weather enough outside without bringing it under the towel.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another thin shaving off the stubborn side. | Beautiful grain for a very modest voyage.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've brought my thoughts back to the landing to hear you.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a known voice above the sound of the cup.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : My knife is put away, so there's time for talk.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I can be plain without putting my private pages out for inspection.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I work at #self.workplace#. Warm water, ready cloth and decent footing all take attention.
dlg @2 resident.job : I prefer work where my hands and my intentions are equally clean.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The words I heard through the steam were #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the whole extent of what I'm prepared to pass.
dlg @1 resident.bye : A sheltered, level bit of pavement home to you.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you test a pocket ship? -> small_hull
node small_hull
say A dipping cup and a shallow breath. It tells me quite plainly if I've left one side heavier.
free
choice What if it sails in a circle? -> small_hull_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node small_hull_again
say I can launch it again without getting up. Not every error is inconvenient.
choice I'll wait for the fleet to grow. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
